{
  "id": "salinity_of_water",
  "title": "Salinity of Water",
  "description": "Salinity - salt content - of fresh, brackish and sea water. Calculate and analyze dissolved salt content in various water types.",
  "type": "chart-table",
  "components": [
    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "content": "# Salinity of Water\n\nSalinity is the saltiness or measure of dissolved salt in water.\n\n**Standard Conversion:**\n- 35 g dissolved salt / kg sea water = 35 ppt = 35 o/oo = 3.5% = 35000 ppm = 35000 mg/l\n\n## Water Type Classifications by Salinity (ppm)\n\n| Water Type | Salinity Range (ppm) |\n|---|---|\n| Fresh Water (City Water) | < 100 |\n| Water Supply | < 500 |\n| Drinking Water (US Limit) | < 1,000 |\n| Agriculture Irrigation | < 2,000 |\n| Brackish Water (Mild) | 1,000 - 5,000 |\n| Brackish Water (Moderate) | 5,000 - 15,000 |\n| Brackish Water (Heavy) | 15,000 - 35,000 |\n| Seawater | 30,000 - 50,000 |\n| Brine | > 50,000 |\n| Dead Sea | 330,000 |"
    },
    {
      "type": "calculator",
      "inputs": [
        {
          "id": "salt_concentration",
          "label": "Salt Concentration",
          "type": "number",
          "unit": "ppm",
          "defaultValue": 35000
        }
      ],
      "outputs": [
        {
          "id": "ppt",
          "label": "Salinity (ppt)",
          "formula": "inputs.salt_concentration / 1000",
          "unit": "ppt"
        },
        {
          "id": "percent",
          "label": "Salinity (%)",
          "formula": "inputs.salt_concentration / 10000",
          "unit": "%",
          "format": "decimal"
        },
        {
          "id": "mg_per_liter",
          "label": "Concentration",
          "formula": "inputs.salt_concentration",
          "unit": "mg/l",
          "format": "decimal"
        },
        {
          "id": "grams_per_kg",
          "label": "Dissolved Salt",
          "formula": "inputs.salt_concentration / 1000",
          "unit": "g/kg",
          "format": "decimal"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
